  "record": {
    "read_status": "full",
    "file_problem": "Full paper text is present.",
    "relation": "uses_without_test",
    "tranche": "T4",
    "tranche_reason": "Reports test-accuracy results for SAM-based and other federated-learning methods on image datasets with heterogeneous client splits and different architectures. It does not test any listed version directly.",
    "gate_note": "The paper reports test accuracy for federated methods and ablations. These findings bear on generalization in a federated setting, but do not test the claim versions’ specified phenomena. Table values are recorded as rows and mapped to versions [\"none\"].",
    "test_reason": "The study uses the flat-minima/generalization premise to design FedTOGA and evaluates federated algorithms and ablations. It does not test V1–V8. In particular, it does not measure magnitude-aware sharpness against training–test gaps or compare its rankings with other measures (V7). FedAdam/FedYogi comparisons concern adaptive server aggregation with client SGD, without the optimizer comparison and tuning conditions specified in V4.",
    "authors_conclusion": "The record's paraphrase is accurate: the authors conclude that global-update estimates of perturbations and corrections to local dynamic regularizers improve global/local consistency, accuracy, and convergence. They also claim no additional local storage or uplink communication overhead and an O(1/T) convergence rate under their assumptions.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "Federated learning with client-local optimization, partial participation, heterogeneous data, SAM-based perturbation and dynamic regularization; not the centralized settings in the claim versions.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Reported accuracy varies with dataset, model, client data partition and participation rate. The paper also studies sensitivity to learning-rate decay and FedTOGA coefficients.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "FedTOGA achieves higher reported test accuracy than the selected federated baselines, and sequential correction modules improve the SAM-only ablation.",
        "proposed_claim": "Global-update corrections to perturbations and dynamic regularization improve accuracy in the tested heterogeneous federated CIFAR settings.",
